From: M1892 mainline bring-up
Subject: firmware: qcom: avoid coherent MP_ASSIGN allocations on M1892

The M1892 secure-world path does not tolerate dma_alloc_coherent() while
starting MPSS.  Physical R78 testing proved that a retained ordinary page,
streaming-mapped during SCM probe, works for both the MP_ASSIGN descriptor
and the SMCCC extended-argument table.

Keep that validated implementation but remove every bring-up trace marker.
This patch is a clean standalone replacement for experimental patches 0009
through 0014; do not apply it on top of that series.

The real QCOM_SCM_MP_ASSIGN call and all memory-protection semantics remain
unchanged.  The special path is restricted to the meizu,m1892 root
compatible.

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm-smc.c b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm-smc.c
index 574930729..40d28db58 100644
